{"14093":{"aka":["Church of St Laurence and St James","St. Laurence's Church, Long Eaton"],"h":16,"osm":"way/53805087","kind":"church","listEntry":1204249,"listUrl":"https://historicengland.org.uk/listing/the-list/list-entry/1204249","qid":"Q7589457","image":"http://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/St%20Laurence%27s%20Church%2C%20Long%20Eaton%2C%20from%20Market%20Place%20%282%263%29.jpg","article":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St_Laurence%27s_Church,_Long_Eaton","cat":"St. Laurence's Church, Long Eaton","stories":[{"layer":"longeaton","text":"Domesday Book calls the village Aitone. Its church of St Laurence stands east of the Market Place: local tradition dates parts of it to the 11th century and King Cnut, but its oldest parts may be from after the Conquest, in the 12th century. It was a daughter church of Sawley until the 19th century. It is listed Grade II*.","source":{"title":"Long Eaton","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Long_Eaton","kind":"Wikipedia"},"when":"12th century","whenSrc":{"title":"Long Eaton","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Long_Eaton","kind":"Wikipedia"},"nm":"St Laurence's, Long Eaton"}],"sum":"St. Laurence's Church, Long Eaton, is a Grade II* listed parish church in Long Eaton, England. 11th century","sumSrc":{"title":"St Laurence's Church, Long Eaton","kind":"Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St_Laurence%27s_Church%2C_Long_Eaton"},"open":[{"what":"place of worship","web":"https://www.st-laurence.net/"}],"council":"Erewash Borough Council","xy":[-1.27065,52.89882]},"281675":{"aka":["Church of St Wilfrid"],"y":1220,"f":"century","src":"Historic England (via Wikipedia)","dt":"Early 13th century","h":16,"osm":"way/195210078","kind":"church","listEntry":1235903,"listUrl":"https://historicengland.org.uk/listing/the-list/list-entry/1235903","qid":"Q15979520","image":"http://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/St%20Wilfrids%20Church%2C%20Calverton%20-%20geograph.org.uk%20-%201758901.jpg","article":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St_Wilfrid%27s_Church,_Calverton","cat":"St Wilfrid's Church, Calverton","stories":[{"layer":"calverton","text":"The village appears as Calvretone in the Domesday survey of 1086, with a church and a priest. St Wilfrid's Church dates mostly from the 14th century; its nave and tower were rebuilt in 1760–63 and its chancel in 1835, and it was restored in 1881.","source":{"title":"Calverton, Nottinghamshire","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calverton,_Nottinghamshire","kind":"Wikipedia"},"when":"1086","whenSrc":{"title":"Calverton, Nottinghamshire","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calverton,_Nottinghamshire","kind":"Wikipedia"},"nm":"Calvretone"}],"sum":"St Wilfrid's Church is a Grade II* listed parish church in the Church of England in Calverton, Nottinghamshire.","sumSrc":{"title":"St Wilfrid's Church, Calverton","kind":"Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St_Wilfrid%27s_Church%2C_Calverton"},"council":"Gedling Borough Council","xy":[-1.08072,53.03641]}}